# Clarify Before Acting

Do not start implementing, planning in depth, or making irreversible changes when important context is missing. Ask first — in every mode (Agent, Plan, Ask, Debug, or otherwise).

## When to ask

Ask before proceeding if any of the following are unclear:

- Goal, success criteria, or constraints
- Scope (what is in vs out)
- Preferred approach when multiple valid options exist
- Target files, APIs, designs, copy, or data the user did not provide
- Acceptance criteria that would change the output meaningfully

## How to ask

- Ask focused questions early (batch related ones in one turn)
- Prefer concrete options when helpful (A vs B) over open-ended prompts
- State what you will assume only if the user wants you to proceed without answering
- After answers, confirm understanding briefly, then act

## Examples

```
❌ BAD: User says "improve the hero" → immediately rewrite layout and copy
✅ GOOD: Ask which goal (conversion, clarity, brand), constraints, and whether copy may change

❌ BAD: User says "add auth" → scaffold a full auth stack
✅ GOOD: Ask provider preference, session vs JWT, and which pages need protection
```

## Exception

If the request is already specific enough to produce a correct result, proceed without ritual questions. Do not delay obvious, well-scoped work.
